From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: finalpantasy <finalpantasy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:45:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/34] d3d11 interp: record the blend context on a worker
 thread

The render thread makes each context call on the main recording context and
queues a copy for the blend context (arrays and upload data copied,
interfaces held by reference until replayed). Constant-buffer blending, the
dynamic-buffer prefill and the blend list's FinishCommandList run on the
worker. The presenter waits for the blend list by ticket, and the game waits
only until the presenter has taken the previous frame, not until it has shown
it; mid-frame syncs wait for the presenter first to keep frame order.
Getters read the main context only (they leaked references from the blend
one). Devices are not created SINGLETHREADED while recording.

FFXII_D3D_INTERP_KICK_KB and FFXII_D3D_INTERP_SPIN_US tune the queue; the
paced report gives presenter and game wait times per frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
